AYN Thor Qualcomm Sensor Core data

The sensor registry inputs in this directory were recovered from the stock
AYN Thor Android BSP. They select the Kailua HDK SH5001 profile while leaving
calibration state writable and persistent under /userdata.

Stock Android build: Thor_V1.0.0.377_20260206_165408_user
Hardware platform: HDK
SoC ID: 603 (QCS8550)
Physical IMU: Senodia SH5001

Runtime path
------------

The ADSP/QSH firmware owns the SH5001. hexagonrpcd exposes the QSH file
services, libqmi/libssc receives SSC reports over QRTR, and ssccli provides a
raw accelerometer/gyroscope smoke test. The generated registry and learned
per-unit calibration live under /userdata/system/qcom-sensors/thor and are
never overwritten automatically.

The SM8550 device tree already enables the Thor-specific ADSP firmware and
the upstream non-secure ADSP FastRPC channel. S28qcom-sensors generates the
registry with the stock HDK/603 filters, starts SensorsPD before RootPD, and
accepts either /dev/fastrpc-adsp or /dev/fastrpc-adsp-secure.

Motion bridge
-------------

S29qcom-motion exposes the built-in accelerometer and gyroscope as DSU/Cemuhook
slot 0 on 127.0.0.1:26760. Configgen enables the source for supported emulators
only while the bridge readiness marker exists.

The initial Thor coordinate profile uses the same landscape gamepad mapping
as the Odin 3. Its direction, sensitivity, and long-running drift still require
validation on a Thor booted into Batocera before the profile can be considered
final.

Run `batocera-qcom-motion --check` for a DSU packet check, or
`batocera-qcom-sensors-test 5` to validate the complete sensor stack.

Calibration
-----------

Launch "Motion Sensor Calibration" from the Tools system with the Thor resting
still. Calibration is stored separately in
/userdata/system/qcom-sensors/thor/motion-calibration.ini.
